id=a52sxq_settings_search_reindex
name=Settings search: re-index after every ROM build
author=kusti420
description=UNTESTED-ON-DEVICE. SecSettingsIntelligence only rebuilds its search index when Build.FINGERPRINT (a boolean key in shared_prefs/indexing_manager.xml), the locale or a provider's versionCode changes. Our fingerprint is the S26U's (S948BXXS4BZIG) on every build and SecSettings' versionCode is always 37, so the index built at the first boot after a data wipe (2026-10-09 22:45) was never rebuilt: preferences added by later builds were never indexed, e.g. Display > Screen resolution (unica_screen_resolution, added 2026-10-10), so "resolution" only found the disabled stock screen_resolution row. The full-index check and the "indexed" marker now use Build.DISPLAY (ro.build.display.id, unique per build), so the first search after flashing a new build rebuilds the index once, as a stock OTA does. Also adds "Refresh rate, Hz" to the English search keywords of Display > Motion smoothness (stock keyword is only "Motion smoothness", so "refresh" found nothing).
